+# Philosophy
+
+For whoever proposes adding a service, a dependency or a store to larder. It holds the tenets that guide the
+decisions: what the team favors when options conflict. Written after the same argument for a new service came up a
+third time in 2025 and Nadia asked for it to be written down so a proposal starts from it instead of rediscovering it.
+
+## Tenets
+
+### Larder runs one database and one web app
+
+A new service is rejected unless it does something Postgres cannot, and at least two volunteers can restore it; a
+hosted service nobody has to run, such as the card gateway, is not a new service under this tenet. It rules out
+adding a service for speed or convenience alone when Postgres can be made to do the job, and it rules out a service
+only one volunteer knows how to run. Applied in
+[keep sessions in the database](adr/0001-keep-sessions-in-the-database.md),
+[run background jobs on Postgres](adr/0002-run-background-jobs-on-postgres.md) and
+[search pantry items in Postgres](adr/0003-search-pantry-items-in-postgres.md).
